## Task
Write claims for this section using ONLY the evidence above, exactly as for any other section: every claim
must cite the chunk_id of the `<evidence>` tag it came from. If the evidence does not support a claim, do
not write it.

In addition, extract distinct audience personas from the evidence. Each persona is a named archetype of the
brand's audience (e.g. "Weekend warrior", "Budget-conscious parent"), not just a demographic label. For each
persona, provide:
- name: a short, descriptive label for this persona
- pain_points: problems or frustrations this persona has, per the evidence
- interests: what this persona cares about or values, per the evidence
- chunk_ids: every evidence chunk_id this persona is built from

Only extract a persona if the evidence supports both pain_points and interests -- an incomplete or
speculative persona is worse than none. If the evidence is insufficient to build any persona, output an
empty personas list rather than inventing one.

## Output
Return claims (section, text, chunk_id) as usual, plus a separate list of personas (name, pain_points,
interests, chunk_ids).
